      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "1. "
        ],
        [
          "Core Concept",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-802c-b3d4-f176782ce742",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The "
        ],
        [
          "@SpringBootApplication",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " annotation is like the \"main switch\" that tells Spring Boot to start your application. It bundles together three important features: setting up Spring configuration, enabling component scanning, and allowing Spring Boot's auto-configuration. Without it, you'd need to configure everything manually."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80bd-ade3-fb598c73d31a",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Think of it like a "
        ],
        [
          "constructor in C++ that also initializes all dependencies, sets up defaults, and scans for components to build your application",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80b9-a96d-c9950df0c81c",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8000-bc27-cedbdf246870",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "2. "
        ],
        [
          "Key Interview Points",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8051-bd03-edd0bb9b2e4a",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "✅ "
        ],
        [
          "@SpringBootApplication",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " is a "
        ],
        [
          "meta-annotation",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " combining:"
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80e1-ab34-f92840a2a174",
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "richText": [
            [
              "@Configuration",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " (marks the class as a source of Spring configuration)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "20824eb1-ed54-806d-83e7-f1495e39b1ae",
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "richText": [
            [
              "@EnableAutoConfiguration",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " (lets Spring Boot configure things automatically based on the classpath)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "20824eb1-ed54-800b-9e47-cbbc406372c8",
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "richText": [
            [
              "@ComponentScan",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " (automatically finds classes annotated with "
            ],
            [
              "@Component",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              ", "
            ],
            [
              "@Service",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              ", etc.)"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-805a-a759-eced312a8b8a",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "✅ It must be placed on a "
        ],
        [
          "main class",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " — the one with the "
        ],
        [
          "main()",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " method that runs your Spring Boot application."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80d0-9b7f-d4482817541f",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "✅ Interviewers often ask about what this annotation combines, how Spring Boot does auto-configuration, and how component scanning works."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80ea-b39b-c530b66dbc74",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "✅ It "
        ],
        [
          "reduces boilerplate code",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and helps developers get started quickly without needing deep configuration knowledge at the beginning."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-805d-a4c0-db5b4a726b18",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8030-960a-ddcc029a753c",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "3. "
        ],
        [
          "Code Example",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8076-b9dd-c510de561f1b",
      "type": "code",
      "richText": [
        [
          "// File: DemoApplication.java\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication  // <--- This is the key annotation!\npublic class DemoApplication {\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);  // Starts the app\n    }\n}\n"
        ]
      ],
      "language": "Java"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8058-bdf4-f05c79125da6",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "What happens here:"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-809f-8f9f-c4d464776dec",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot looks for other components (like Controllers, Services, etc.) in the same package or sub-packages."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80be-8c4f-c6d9cfa0a5db",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It auto-configures beans (objects managed by Spring) like DataSource, Tomcat, etc., based on what’s in your classpath."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80a6-95b1-df6152f08c1d",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It wires everything together, just like C++ constructors linking dependencies."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80fb-a467-ff5f90f2eb15",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8082-8afc-cbc342ac07ea",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "4. "
        ],
        [
          "Common Interview Questions",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
