    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-809d-938a-fbee5993c91e",
      "type": "quote",
      "richText": [
        [
          "\"What is @SpringBootApplication and why is it important?\""
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8059-a325-f7b197526f40",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Answer",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ":"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-804b-a711-f8d92e8155aa",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "\""
        ],
        [
          "@SpringBootApplication",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " is a convenience annotation in Spring Boot that combines "
        ],
        [
          "@Configuration",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", "
        ],
        [
          "@ComponentScan",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", and "
        ],
        [
          "@EnableAutoConfiguration",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ". It marks the main class of a Spring Boot app and sets up automatic configuration and component scanning. It simplifies project setup by reducing boilerplate and allowing Spring to auto-configure beans based on the classpath. It’s essential because it enables Spring Boot’s core features with a single annotation.\"**"
        ]
      ]
    },
